    36	## 1. Statement, conventions, and what is consumable
    37	
    38	`F=(P,Q):C^2->C^2` is a Keller map (`J:=Jac F ∈ C^*`), not an automorphism,
    39	geometric degree `N=d=[C(x,y):Frac C[P,Q]] >= 2`. `A_F` is Jelonek's
    40	non-properness curve. On a smooth compactification `X` of `C^2` on which `F`
    41	extends to `Phi: X -> P^2`, the boundary splits (Orevkov §2) into `L_∞`
    42	(components sent into the target line at infinity), `L_C` (components on which
    43	`Phi` is constant with finite value) and `L_F` (components on which `Phi` is
    44	non-constant with affine image). Components `l ⊆ L_F` are the **map-dicriticals
    45	with affine image**; `l' := l ∩ Phi^{-1}(C^2)`, `D_l := Phi(l')` a component of
    46	`A_F`, `s_l := deg(l' -> D_l)`, `mu_l` the generic local degree of `Phi` along
    47	`l`. Orevkov's collapsed model is `f*: X~* -> X* = C^2 ∪ {∞}`, a proper
    48	constant-multiplicity branched covering of degree `N` with `(f*)^{-1}(∞)={∞}`;
    49	`mu_x f*` is the local multiplicity at `x ∈ X~*` (Orevkov §4, `refs/jc86.pdf`
    50	p. 6). Write `corr_l := sum_{x ∈ l', mu_x != mu_l} (mu_x f* - mu_l f*) >= 0`.
    51	
    52	**Consumed as theorems** (from the charged integration `69970f4d`, §1):
    53	the `Y=Spec B` construction and four boxes (in particular `a_D >= 1` on every
    54	component `D` of `A_F`, and box `(U,e>1)` empty); the covering lemma and
    55	conversion law `a_p=s_p-b_p`; **Lemma 4.2** `e_j = 1 + v_j(dx∧dy)`; the `chi_c`
    56	toolkit and the Euler identity **(E)** `1 = d(1-chi_c(A_F)) + chi_c(F^{-1}(A_F))`;
    57	the dictionary `e_j=mu_l`, `delta_j=s_l`, `a=f(z)` (integration §9). **Not
    58	consumed** (these are what is under proof): `A_F=B`, H2 (`A_F` irreducible),
    59	H3, `b=0`, `f(z)=2`, and any component-wise copy of (M′).
