   190	> **Lemma 3.1 (branch locus).** Put `Br := ∪_{l : mu_l >= 2} D_l`. Then `q` is
   191	> finite étale over `C^2 - Br`, and `Br != ∅`.
   192	> *Proof.* `q` is étale at every point of `U` (Keller) and at the generic point
   193	> of `B_j` exactly when `e_j=1` (flat + fibre-reduced ⟹ unramified ⟹ étale).
   194	> Hence the branch locus has codimension-one part exactly `Br`; by purity of the
   195	> branch locus (Zariski–Nagata; `C^2` regular, `Y` normal, `q` finite) the branch
   196	> locus is pure of codimension one or empty, so it equals `Br`. If `Br=∅` then
   197	> `q` is finite étale over the simply connected `C^2` with `Y` irreducible, so
   198	> `d=1`. ∎
