   301	
   302	> **Corollary 3.7 (Orevkov's inequality is strict under H2).** If `A_F` is
   303	> irreducible then `sum_{l} mu_l <= N-2`; equivalently `sum_l corr_l >= 1`;
   304	> equivalently (by [Z-6.5b]) `A_F` carries at least one **non-immersive** point,
   305	> i.e. a locally irreducible singularity of some `Phi(l')`.
   306	> *Proof.* Suppose `sum_l mu_l = N-1`. By [O-4.2] Cor. 4.3 this is exactly the
   307	> equality case, so every `corr_l = 0`. All dicriticals map onto the irreducible
   308	> `A_F`, so `a = N - sum_l s_l mu_l <= N - sum_l mu_l = 1` (using `s_l >= 1`),
   309	> and `a >= 1` forces `a = 1` and `s_l = 1` for every `l`. Then `2a = 2 <= N`,
   310	> and Theorem 3.5(ii) applies. ∎
   311	
   312	> **Corollary 3.8 (Orevkov's closing Remark, reproved).** No component of `L_F`
   313	> has `mu_l f^* = N-1`.
   314	> *Proof.* If `mu_{l_1} = N-1` then [O-4.2] forces every other term of the budget
   315	> to vanish, so `l_1` is the only dicritical and `corr_{l_1}=0`; hence `A_F` is
   316	> irreducible and `sum_l mu_l = N-1`, contradicting Cor. 3.7. ∎
   317	
   318	Corollary 3.8 recovers, with a complete proof, the assertion Orevkov states as
   319	an unproved Remark ("repeating the above arguments…", `jc86.pdf` p. 10) and that
   320	Domrina–Orevkov cite as `[3, remark after 5.3]` (`do.pdf` p. 6). It is a
   321	first-class sanity gate on the machine of §3.
   322	
   323	<!-- SECTION 3 END -->
   324	
   325	## 4. Route 3 — Unique-versus-mixed at N=4
   326	
   327	### 4.1 The complete profile list
   328	
   329	By [O-4.2] the budget is an **equality**: `sum_l (mu_l + corr_l) = N-1 = 3`,
   330	each summand `>= 1`. Writing profiles as multisets of pairs `(mu_l, corr_l)`,
   331	the complete list at `N=4` is
   332	
   333	| # dicriticals | profile | contains `mu=1`? |
   334	|---|---|---|
   335	| 1 | `(3,0)` | no |
   336	| 1 | `(2,1)` | no |
   337	| 1 | `(1,2)` | **yes** — (c) |
   338	| 2 | `(2,0)+(1,0)` | **yes** — (d) |
   339	| 2 | `(1,1)+(1,0)` | **yes** — (e) |
   340	| 3 | `(1,0)+(1,0)+(1,0)` | **yes** — (f) |
   341	
   342	Row `(3,0)` is excluded outright by Cor. 3.8 (Orevkov's Remark, here proved).
   343	Row `(2,1)` carries no trivial dicritical and is the profile that survives all
   344	arguments in this report; it is the promoted `a=2`, `(delta,e)=(1,2)`,
   345	`b=0` row of SHEET-GATE Thm 4.4.
   346	
   347	### 4.2 Rows (c), (e), (f): killed by the branch locus
   348	
   349	> **Proposition 4.1.** Profiles (c), (e), (f) are impossible.
   350	> *Proof.* In each of them every dicritical has `mu_l = 1`, so `Br = ∅` in the
   351	> sense of Lemma 3.1 — and Lemma 3.1 gives `N = 1`. ∎
   352	
   353	This is the numbered replacement the brief asked for. Domrina–Orevkov dismiss the
   354	unique-`mu=1` case (our row (c)) with the sentence "If the ramification order is
   355	1 then `F` is an unbranched covering over `C^2`. This is also impossible."
   356	(`do.pdf` p. 6, §2). As the registry flagged (R12), that sentence is **not** a
   357	verbatim Orevkov theorem: at `N=4` a unique `mu=1` dicritical is forced by
   358	[O-4.2] to carry `corr = 2`, so `f^*` is *not* unbranched over all of `C^2` —
   359	it is unbranched only over the complement of one or two points. Their conclusion
   360	is nevertheless correct, by either of two complete arguments: topologically,
   361	`C^2` minus a finite set is still simply connected, so a connected `4`-fold
   362	covering of it is impossible; algebraically, Prop. 4.1 above, which never
   363	mentions the correction points at all because purity of the branch locus
   364	(Zariski–Nagata) rules out isolated branch points a priori. **The author
   365	inference flagged at R12/Chain C is hereby discharged.**
   366	
   367	### 4.3 Row (d): the mixed remainder
   368	
   369	Row (d) is the transposition-horn case. Its numerics: one dicritical `l_1` with
   370	`mu_1 = 2`, one `l_0` with `mu_0 = 1`, and `corr_1 = corr_0 = 0`, so [O-5.2] and
   371	Lemma 3.3 apply to **both**: every branch of `Phi(l_1')` and of `Phi(l_0')` at
   372	every affine point is smooth. That is exactly the rigidity the brief asked for:
   373	`corr_l = 0` at a trivial dicritical means the parametrisation `l_0' -> D_0` is
   374	an **immersion with no critical point whatsoever**, so `D_0` has no
   375	locally-irreducible singularity, and likewise for `D_1`.
   376	
   377	> **Theorem 4.2 (`N=4` under H2).** Let `F` be a noninvertible Keller map of
