   381	> `G = S_4`, and **(M) holds verbatim at rank four in the transposition class**.
   382	> *Proof.* Rows (c), (e), (f) die by Prop. 4.1. Row (d) with `A_F` irreducible
   383	> has every `corr_l = 0`, hence `sum_l mu_l = 3 = N-1`, contradicting Cor. 3.7.
   384	> Row `(3,0)` dies by Cor. 3.8. Only `(2,1)` survives; over the irreducible
   385	> `A_F`, `a + s_1·2 = 4` with `a >= 1` gives `s_1 = 1`, `a = 2`, `b = 0`. ∎
   386	
   387	Theorem 4.2 **refutes the SHEET-GATE Thm 4.4 row `a=1`, `(1,2)+(1,1)`, `b=1`
   388	under H2**, which is the entire content of the charged transposition horn once
   389	`A_F` is known irreducible. It also removes the dependence on the (unproved)
   390	census equality `f(z)=2`: Cor. 4.5 of the SHEET-GATE report is no longer needed.
   391	
   392	### 4.4 Row (d) without H2: the residual configuration
   393	
   394	If `A_F` is *reducible*, row (d) survives with the two dicriticals over
   395	**different** components. Everything about it can be pinned:
