covering of the sphere S with the branching curve K̃ = S̃ ∩ l∗ . Let K = f ∗ (K̃).
It follows from the assumption µx f ∗ = µl f ∗ that f ∗ −1 (K) = K̃ and that f ∗ |S̃−K̃
                                                                  def
is an unbranched covering of S − K and hence, H = π1 (S̃ − K̃) is a subgroup of
                               def
finite index of the group G = π1 (S − K).
