codex
A decisive obstruction has emerged: ordinary plane degree is not invariant under the very target automorphisms that preserve every promoted residual datum. If one residual map existed, postcomposition by \((u,v)\mapsto(u,v+u^k)\) would keep \(N=4\), both dicritical profiles, all fibre counts, and all monodromy/singularity data, while sending \(\deg D_1\) to infinity. I’m therefore typing the raw-degree goal as structurally unbounded and sharpening the replacement target to an automorphism-minimal degree/polar-order invariant. The Chau route still gives a genuine fixed-coordinate ratio constraint.
